## COMMUNICATION
An oxygen-assisted cathodic deposition of zeolitic imidazolate frameworks (ZIFs) is reported herein. This cathodic process is triggered by the electrochemical reduction reaction of oxygen, operable cost-effectively in the absence of supporting electrolyte, and capable of producing large-area ZIF films with uniform but tunable thickness.
